<Base title="About YCG" description="An independent initiative built from lived experience to make life in Canada easier to understand."><section class="page-heading wrap"><span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CLARITY CAN CHANGE A BEGINNING</span><h1>Built for the questions<br/>you didn't know to ask.</h1><p class="intro">Your Canada Guide is an independent initiative, founded by Mary C. Nwosu to make unfamiliar systems easier to navigate. We bring official information and community resources together with plain-language explanations and clear next steps.</p></section><section class="wrap about-grid"><img src="/images/new-chapter.webp" srcset="/images/new-chapter-480.webp 480w, /images/new-chapter-800.webp 800w, /images/new-chapter.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 560px) calc(100vw - 40px), (max-width: 1280px) 45vw, 560px" alt="Illustration of newcomers connecting with a neighbour" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy"/><div><span class="badge coral">Our mission</span><h2>Make life in Canada easier to understand.</h2><p>We connect plain-language explanations with the organizations and sources behind them, so you can make sense of your options and choose a next step.</p><h3>The future we want to contribute to</h3><p>A Canada where being unfamiliar with the system does not leave a newcomer at a disadvantage.</p><a class="text-link" href="/our-story/">Read the founder's story →</a></div></section><section class="section wrap"><div class="section-heading"><h2>How we want to help</h2></div><div class="value-grid"><div><h3>Clarity without assumptions</h3><p>Explain the steps, unfamiliar terms, and questions to ask. Let people begin without knowing a program's name.</p></div><div><h3>Trust with visible limits</h3><p>Show sources, location, and review information. Say when something still needs checking.</p></div><div><h3>Independence and dignity</h3><p>Help people make their own decisions. Basic guidance should not create personal obligations.</p></div></div><div class="pills"><a href="/team/">Meet the team →</a><a href="/about/trust/">Trust & sources →</a><a href="/resources/">Find organizations →</a><a href="/about/contact/">Contact & support status →</a></div></section></Base>
